# Public, non-secret config only: every EXPO_PUBLIC_* value is bundled into the app.
# Copy to .env and fill in. See decisions.md Q-02 for RPC reachability.
# Preset CointMU RPC nodes, comma-separated. The first is the default; users can pick another
# or add their own in Settings > Network. Every node must report chain ID EXPO_PUBLIC_CHAIN_ID.
# These three are LAN-only (campus network 10.0.0.0/8 or ZeroTier) and plain HTTP: fine for dev
# builds, but release builds need public HTTPS endpoints (Q-02). Tests and CI use dummy .invalid URLs.
EXPO_PUBLIC_RPC_URLS=http://10.64.24.101:8585,http://10.64.24.106:8585,http://10.64.24.113:8585
EXPO_PUBLIC_CHAIN_ID=1912
# Optional GlitchTip DSN for error reports (D-77): http(s)://<public key>@<host>/<project id>.
# Empty or unset = error reporting is fully off. A DSN is a public, write-only identifier. The
# GlitchTip server is LAN/ZeroTier only today, so reports wait on the phone until it is reachable;
# a plain http:// DSN works in Expo Go and dev builds, release builds need https (as in Q-02).
# EXPO_PUBLIC_GLITCHTIP_DSN=http://publickey@glitchtip.example.invalid/1
# Optional block explorer base URL (Q-27). When set, tx screens link to <url>/tx/<hash>.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_EXPLORER_URL=https://explorer.example.invalid
